
  The plan uses the details they each gave:
  - [1mOrder:[0m newest first, by [38;2;177;185;249mcreatedAt[39m then [38;2;177;185;249mid[39m, because some tasks share a timestamp.
  - [1mLimit:[0m default 20, max 50 (alice, #8).
  - [1mResponse:[0m [38;2;177;185;249m{items, nextCursor}[39m, where [38;2;177;185;249mnextCursor[39m is null when there are no more pages (alice, #8).
  - [1mCursor past the end:[0m returns an empty page (alice, #8).
  - [1mMalformed cursor:[0m returns a 400 (bob, #9).

  One question is still open in the plan: whether a [38;2;177;185;249mlimit[39m above 50 (or not a positive number) gets cut down to 50 or rejected with a 400. Neither of them has said, so I didn't pick one. They can
  settle it in the room or in their card's note.

